   "text": "I'm unable to complete this analysis because the Human Protein Atlas data tools are currently returning connection errors (\"Not connected\") on every request — I've retried repeatedly across all the relevant endpoints (cancer marker search, tissue expression search, protein lookup, subcellular location search, batch lookup), and none are responding.\n\nI don't want to fabricate or estimate any gene lists, p-values, or expression values, so I won't guess at the results.\n\n**What I would have done to answer your question (once the tools are back up):**\n\n1. **Identify the gene set** — Query `search_cancer_markers` for liver hepatocellular carcinoma (TCGA) with `prognostic = unfavorable` to get genes with validated unfavourable prognosis, then intersect those with genes classified as \"tissue enriched\" in liver at the RNA level (RNA consensus tissue classification / enriched flag from HPA).\n\n2. **Bar chart of protein classes** — Pull protein class annotations for each overlapping gene (via `get_protein_classes` / `get_protein_info`) and count membership per class.\n\n3. **Scatter plot** — Plot liver nTPM (x, log scale) against prognostic p-value (y, log scale) with gene labels, using the p-values returned by the prognosis query and nTPM from `get_tissue_expression`.\n\n4. **Heatmap** — Gather nTPM values for liver, kidney, pancreas, colon, and lung for each gene and generate a heatmap.\n\n5. **Table** — Compile gene symbol, protein class(es), prognostic p-value, liver nTPM, and the nTPM values for the five tissues into a table.\n\nPlease try again in a little while, or let me know if there's an alternative data source you'd like me to use. I'd be happy to rerun the full pipeline as soon as the tools are accessible.",
